From 2c172f779cb6c242c2d26e7443670bb4feb32ab3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:54:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/17] feat(mcp): resolve guessed tool-name orderings and name
 close tools

The catalog mixes verb-first (create-feature-flag) and noun-first
(experiment-create) names, singular and plural (actions-get-all next to
action-create), and the exec description's own examples taught the
noun-first pattern. Every task-c benchmark run guessed feature-flag-create
(P12), and the unknown-tool error named no tools although the
instructions promise similar names (P13).

findTool now resolves an alias generated from the catalog itself: one
verb move, one verb synonym (get-all/list, get/retrieve, delete/destroy)
and one singular/plural switch away from a real name. A real name always
wins, and a spelling two tools could answer to is left out, so nothing is
renamed and no alias guesses between tools. An alias of a scope- or
flag-gated tool gets that tool's own refusal.

The unknown-tool error now lists the three closest real names (shared
words, plural- and synonym-insensitive, one-letter typos counted), and
tool-search.md shows the real naming patterns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
